description:
**Location:** rust/lichen-rpl/src/dodag.rs line 323 (process_dio entry)

**Issue:** Root nodes should never process DIOs for parent selection (RFC 6550: root is the DODAG origin, has no parent). The current implementation relies on indirect guards (rank comparison at line 370) rather than explicit rejection.

The existing comment at line 369 describes the rank check as a loop-prevention mechanism, not a root guard. This creates defense-in-depth gaps where edge cases (e.g., fraudulent low ranks) can bypass the intended protection.

**RFC 6550 Section 8.2.2:** "A node that is the DODAG root has the smallest rank in the DODAG, and it is the root of the DODAG."

A root should never select a parent because there is no valid parent with rank < ROOT_RANK.

**Fix:** Add explicit guard at the start of `process_dio`:
```rust
pub fn process_dio(&mut self, dio: &Dio, neighbor_addr: [u8; 16], link_etx: f32) -> DioOutcome {
    // Root nodes never select parents - they are the DODAG origin
    if self.role == DodagRole::Root {
        return DioOutcome::Rejected;
    }
    // ... rest of function
}
```

This is defense-in-depth; the root never needs to evaluate parent candidates.
